```sh
{"body":"**MUST-FIX**: This only links to dependency tasks that already exist in `specToTaskMap` or before the current spec in iteration order. In a single derive pass, if a consumer spec is processed before its depended-on spec, `derive` warns and creates the consumer task without the dependency link, and nothing revisits it later. I reproduced this with `derive --all` after creating `@consumer` before `@base`; `@task-consumer` ended up with `depends_on: []`. That breaks the intended `@cmd-derive ac-17` behavior for same-run derivation.","line":442,"path":"src/cli/commands/derive.ts"}
```
